    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d364">

                <pb facs="0513" n="255" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg255"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gerard</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-06-22">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 22, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1862. Your 2434, June 15. Proposed exchange of cotton for dyestuffs is but an
                    isolated feature of the general question of protecting neutral trade which now
                    engages the Department’s attention.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Osborne</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
